WEBVTT

1
00:00:06,458 --> 00:00:09,000
[lively drum tapping]

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,333
[mysterious music playing]

3
00:00:22,958 --> 00:00:25,916
["Let's Swim" by Stela Campos
& Érico Theobaldo playing]

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
-[water splashes]
-[people chatter]

5
00:01:00,833 --> 00:01:04,166
<i>♪ You might think that I'm the stranger ♪</i>

6
00:01:04,250 --> 00:01:07,541
<i>♪ You might think but you don't know me ♪</i>

7
00:01:08,625 --> 00:01:12,333
[boy narrator] <i>I never understood why in</i>
The Little Mermaid <i>Ariel traded the ocean</i>

8
00:01:12,416 --> 00:01:13,875
<i>for a boring prince.</i>

9
00:01:13,958 --> 00:01:15,291
<i>I love being in the water.</i>

10
00:01:15,375 --> 00:01:17,833
<i>♪Might think but you don't know me ♪</i>

11
00:01:17,916 --> 00:01:21,041
<i>♪ You might think that you can't hurt me ♪</i>

12
00:01:21,125 --> 00:01:23,125
{\an8}<i>♪ Just look at me ♪</i>

13
00:01:24,166 --> 00:01:26,375
{\an8}[boy narrator] <i>At least, I used to.</i>

14
00:01:28,208 --> 00:01:32,291
{\an8}<i>♪ Oh oh oh</i>
<i>I'll never let you down ♪</i>

15
00:01:35,083 --> 00:01:37,291
{\an8}<i>♪ Oh oh oh ♪</i>

16
00:01:38,041 --> 00:01:41,958
{\an8}-[bell rings]
<i>-♪ I will know you swim like a dolphin ♪</i>

17
00:01:43,541 --> 00:01:45,000
{\an8}[boy narrator] <i>I am fat.</i>

18
00:01:45,083 --> 00:01:48,500
{\an8}<i>I'm not cute and chubby, I am huge.</i>

19
00:01:49,708 --> 00:01:51,291
{\an8}<i>I take up space.</i>

20
00:01:54,875 --> 00:01:58,416
{\an8}-Everyone an earthquake!
-[people shouting]

21
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:00,458
{\an8}Make way! Make way!
The earthquake's coming!

22
00:02:00,541 --> 00:02:03,250
{\an8}[boy narrator] <i>A whole month away</i>
<i>from this school.</i>

23
00:02:03,333 --> 00:02:05,583
{\an8}<i>Jeez, it's gonna be tough.</i>

24
00:02:05,666 --> 00:02:07,750
{\an8}<i>I don't know how I'll make it.</i>

25
00:02:07,833 --> 00:02:10,208
{\an8}<i>♪ I'll never let you down ♪</i>

26
00:02:10,291 --> 00:02:13,666
{\an8}[boy narrator] <i>Here are a few of</i>
<i>the reasons I'll miss this school so much.</i>

27
00:02:13,750 --> 00:02:17,041
{\an8}<i>♪ Oh oh</i>
<i>You never let me down ♪</i>

28
00:02:19,083 --> 00:02:21,916
{\an8}[boy narrator] <i>Reason number one.</i>
<i>It's such an inclusive environment.</i>

29
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,833
{\an8}LARDASS
TODAY IS THE DAY

30
00:02:24,916 --> 00:02:27,166
{\an8}[students chatter and laugh]

31
00:02:29,458 --> 00:02:31,583
{\an8}Did you hear Marcelo kissed
Felipe at the front gate?

32
00:02:31,666 --> 00:02:33,875
{\an8}Was it Hot Felipe or Fat Felipe?

33
00:02:33,958 --> 00:02:35,375
{\an8}[boy narrator] <i>Reason number two.</i>

34
00:02:36,083 --> 00:02:38,916
{\an8}<i>I just feel so loved and appreciated here.</i>

35
00:02:40,708 --> 00:02:41,875
{\an8}[whistle blows]

36
00:02:43,250 --> 00:02:45,000
{\an8}All right, let's go. Fatso, come on.

37
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:49,125
{\an8}You like playing with balls, right?

38
00:02:49,208 --> 00:02:50,458
{\an8}[boy 1 chuckles]

39
00:02:52,666 --> 00:02:54,666
{\an8}[boy 2] This is gonna suck.

40
00:02:54,750 --> 00:02:56,458
{\an8}[boy narrator] <i>Reason number three.</i>

41
00:02:56,541 --> 00:02:59,416
{\an8}<i>It's the best place</i>
<i>to deal with my anxiety.</i>

42
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:01,791
{\an8}-[boy 3] Goal!
-[students shout]

43
00:03:01,875 --> 00:03:05,000
{\an8}<i>♪ Oh oh</i>
<i>Through these emotions ♪</i>

44
00:03:05,083 --> 00:03:09,791
{\an8}[boy narrator] <i>You see, in this wonderful,</i>
<i>idyllic, flawless paradise,</i>

45
00:03:09,875 --> 00:03:11,875
{\an8}<i>being fat really isn't a problem.</i>

46
00:03:11,958 --> 00:03:15,833
{\an8}BASED ON THE NOVEL BY VITOR MARTINS

47
00:03:16,916 --> 00:03:19,458
<i>A whole vacation away from this place.</i>

48
00:03:22,458 --> 00:03:26,416
<i>Ah, I can finally be alone</i>
<i>without anyone bothering me.</i>

49
00:03:27,250 --> 00:03:30,458
<i>And the best part is, I don't have</i>
<i>to set foot outside the house.</i>

50
00:03:30,541 --> 00:03:31,750
[exhales deeply]

51
00:03:32,625 --> 00:03:35,708
HERE THE WHOLE TIME

52
00:03:35,791 --> 00:03:37,250
<i>I can do whatever I want.</i>

53
00:03:37,333 --> 00:03:39,083
<i>Play video games, read manga,</i>

54
00:03:39,166 --> 00:03:40,875
<i>take afternoon naps</i>

55
00:03:40,958 --> 00:03:43,625
<i>and appreciate the best</i>
<i>that streaming has to offer.</i>

56
00:03:44,166 --> 00:03:46,041
"Your Heart is My Destiny."

57
00:03:46,875 --> 00:03:49,833
-Looks like a terrible movie. I love it.
-[electronic bleep]

58
00:03:49,916 --> 00:03:51,875
[emotional music playing]

59
00:03:51,958 --> 00:03:53,041
<i>My love,</i>

60
00:03:53,125 --> 00:03:56,291
<i>I've replayed this moment</i>
<i>a thousand times in my mind,</i>

61
00:03:56,375 --> 00:03:57,750
<i>and it never feels right.</i>

62
00:03:57,833 --> 00:04:01,750
<i>Walking away feels like</i>
<i>losing something I'll never find again.</i>

63
00:04:04,375 --> 00:04:07,625
<i>If any part of you still wonders</i>
<i>what we could've been,</i>

64
00:04:07,708 --> 00:04:09,958
you know where to find me.

65
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:13,541
[whimsical music playing]

66
00:04:13,625 --> 00:04:16,250
[woman chatters over speaker]

67
00:04:18,875 --> 00:04:20,041
Thank you.

68
00:04:22,416 --> 00:04:24,791
[woman continues chattering]

69
00:04:26,708 --> 00:04:28,916
Wait! Wait!

70
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,083
Don't get on this bus!

71
00:04:32,166 --> 00:04:34,208
[boy narrator] <i>I wish life</i>
<i>was like a romantic comedy.</i>

72
00:04:34,291 --> 00:04:37,041
<i>Just take off your glasses</i>
<i>and automatically become beautiful.</i>

73
00:04:37,125 --> 00:04:39,500
I have one last thing… to say to you.

74
00:04:40,791 --> 00:04:43,416
[kissing]

75
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:46,250
[music becomes emotional]

76
00:04:47,333 --> 00:04:51,000
[boy narrator] <i>But in real life,</i>
<i>a hot guy like that would never want me.</i>

77
00:04:58,500 --> 00:05:00,208
[horn honks]

78
00:05:00,291 --> 00:05:02,541
-[music continues]
-[knocking]

79
00:05:02,625 --> 00:05:05,208
[woman] Felipe? Hey.

80
00:05:05,291 --> 00:05:08,250
The weather's so nice.
You sure you don't wanna go to the pool?

81
00:05:08,333 --> 00:05:11,791
-No, Mom, I'm watching a movie right now.
-Why won't you go? Hm?

82
00:05:11,875 --> 00:05:13,500
You know I hate swimming pools.

83
00:05:13,583 --> 00:05:16,625
-"I hate swimming pools."
-Mom! Stop it, Or I'll do it back.

84
00:05:16,708 --> 00:05:19,375
-I will!
-Stop! Come on, you're on vacation.

85
00:05:19,458 --> 00:05:22,375
-If you're gonna stay holed up… Ew!
-[cell phone ringing]

86
00:05:22,458 --> 00:05:26,458
-They'll be here soon. Clean your room.
-Stop, that's embarrassing! Who's coming?

87
00:05:26,541 --> 00:05:28,125
-Wait who?
-Hey, how are you?

88
00:05:28,208 --> 00:05:30,708
Wait, mom. Wait a minute.
Who's on the way?

89
00:05:35,625 --> 00:05:39,458
-[people chatter and scream]
-[moody contemplative music playing]

90
00:06:08,250 --> 00:06:10,375
-[faucet handle squeaks]
-[water running]

91
00:06:10,458 --> 00:06:13,875
♪ <i>The crab is such a sight to see</i>
<i>You're gonna get to </i>♪

92
00:06:13,958 --> 00:06:17,250
♪ <i>Hanging out with old sardines</i>
<i>In conversation </i>♪

93
00:06:17,333 --> 00:06:21,208
♪ <i>I've been dancing</i>
<i>At the sand bar for my whole life </i>♪

94
00:06:21,708 --> 00:06:24,833
<i>♪ And the octopus is still out back</i>
<i>Serve a soda ♪</i>

95
00:06:24,916 --> 00:06:25,958
<i>♪ Dah dah dah ♪</i>

96
00:06:26,041 --> 00:06:29,916
♪ <i>The dolphin is a dancer</i>
<i>He likes to stomp his fins </i>♪

97
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:34,000
<i>♪ And the giant squid</i>
<i>Is always going to spin ♪</i>

98
00:06:34,083 --> 00:06:36,000
<i>♪ The clams all clap their shells ♪</i>

99
00:06:36,083 --> 00:06:38,250
<i>♪ The fish flop around as well </i>♪

100
00:06:38,333 --> 00:06:41,166
♪ <i>The lobsters spin around</i>
<i>and their tails go… </i>♪ [gasps]

101
00:06:41,875 --> 00:06:45,916
♪ <i>Bar, bar, bar</i>
<i>I wanna go to the sandbar ♪</i>

102
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,250
♪ <i>Bar, bar, bar</i>
<i>We're gonna go to the sandbar ♪</i>

103
00:06:49,333 --> 00:06:51,791
<i>♪ We're coming</i>
<i>Bar, bar, bar, we're gonna go to… </i>♪

104
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,791
-[both scream]
-[lively music playing]

105
00:07:02,208 --> 00:07:03,958
[music fades]

106
00:07:05,041 --> 00:07:06,375
What is this guy doing here?

107
00:07:06,458 --> 00:07:10,166
I told you. Didn't I tell you?
Yeah, Sandra's going on vacation.

108
00:07:10,250 --> 00:07:11,458
Mm, a conference for Mauro.

109
00:07:11,541 --> 00:07:13,541
-You didn't tell me.
-Could've sworn I did.

110
00:07:13,625 --> 00:07:16,083
-You didn't ask me, and you--
-Would you like sugar?

111
00:07:16,166 --> 00:07:19,375
No, I like it black. He would stay
with my sister, but something came up.

112
00:07:19,458 --> 00:07:20,958
Oh, well, 15 days will fly by.

113
00:07:21,041 --> 00:07:24,375
15 days? Mom, 15 days? Are you serious?

114
00:07:24,458 --> 00:07:26,416
-This shit was a bad idea.
-[Sandra] Caio Luiz!

115
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:29,208
-I'm so sorry.
-No, I'm sorry. I don't know what to say.

116
00:07:29,291 --> 00:07:31,041
I'm the one who's sorry. Come on.

117
00:07:31,125 --> 00:07:35,375
Let's go. Let's step outside.
You and I are gonna have a little talk.

118
00:07:35,458 --> 00:07:38,250
-[Caio] I'm going. I don't wanna stay.
-[Sandra] Stop complaining. Shh!

119
00:07:38,333 --> 00:07:39,625
I don't want anyone to hear.

120
00:07:39,708 --> 00:07:41,416
15 days is almost the whole vacation.

121
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:44,958
Sweetie, she watered our plants
when we went to the trip to Gramado.

122
00:07:45,041 --> 00:07:47,666
-How can I say no?
-When we got back, they were all dead.

123
00:07:47,750 --> 00:07:49,750
-Right, she overwatered them.
-Yeah.

124
00:07:49,833 --> 00:07:53,250
It'll be good for you. You need to get out
of your room, hang out with people.

125
00:07:53,333 --> 00:07:55,375
-It'll be great.
-I'm staying in my room.

126
00:07:55,458 --> 00:07:57,833
He's 16 years old, he can stay home alone.

127
00:07:57,916 --> 00:07:59,875
Only 16 years old.

128
00:07:59,958 --> 00:08:02,000
Last time I tried
to leave you on your own--

129
00:08:02,083 --> 00:08:05,208
I thought you already punished me.
Now you're trying to ditch me.

130
00:08:05,291 --> 00:08:09,375
You know what? I get it. I also really
don't think it's the best option, I don't.

131
00:08:09,458 --> 00:08:11,375
-Felipe is a little--
-Mom…

132
00:08:11,458 --> 00:08:12,416
What, sweetie?

133
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:14,375
It's not like he tries to hide it.

134
00:08:14,458 --> 00:08:17,833
But this is the best we could get.
And you two already know each other.

135
00:08:17,916 --> 00:08:21,250
No, Mom, we used to. We haven't spoken
in years. He clearly hates me.

136
00:08:21,333 --> 00:08:23,250
Of course I hate him. You saw how he is.

137
00:08:23,333 --> 00:08:25,583
He won't even respond
to "good morning" in the elevator.

138
00:08:25,666 --> 00:08:27,666
[upbeat music playing]

139
00:08:27,750 --> 00:08:28,875
Good morning.

140
00:08:33,833 --> 00:08:35,500
He's one of those gym guys.

141
00:08:35,583 --> 00:08:38,250
-[grunting]
-[lively whimsical music playing]

142
00:08:39,875 --> 00:08:43,208
He's a straight dude who's into dude
stuff, like there's shooter games,

143
00:08:43,291 --> 00:08:44,708
he only reads fantasy.

144
00:08:44,791 --> 00:08:46,166
Mom, he likes football.

145
00:08:46,250 --> 00:08:49,583
-[shouting]
-[energetic techno music playing]

146
00:08:49,666 --> 00:08:51,625
[all cheering]

147
00:08:52,250 --> 00:08:53,500
[whistle blows]

148
00:08:53,583 --> 00:08:56,708
-Worst kind of straight dude.
-Is there a good kind of straight dude?

149
00:08:57,375 --> 00:08:59,958
Don't start cracking jokes
after stabbing me in the back.

150
00:09:00,041 --> 00:09:02,916
I get it, all right?
I understand you don't want to compromise.

151
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,666
You are staying here!
You're staying here, dammit, that's all!

152
00:09:05,750 --> 00:09:07,916
-You're too old to act like this.
-I'm old now?

153
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,708
-Yes, you are too old!
-The bags are already in the car.

154
00:09:10,791 --> 00:09:13,541
Cutting it close to get to the airport.
We've gotta leave now.

155
00:09:13,625 --> 00:09:15,625
-All right.
-[contemplative music playing]

156
00:09:15,708 --> 00:09:16,708
Is there a problem?

157
00:09:16,791 --> 00:09:18,125
-It's fine.
-It's all good.

158
00:09:18,208 --> 00:09:20,708
-Then let's go.
-All right. Say bye to your dad.

159
00:09:20,791 --> 00:09:23,041
-See you.
-Bye, sweetie.

160
00:09:23,625 --> 00:09:26,291
-Behave yourself. Come on.
-Love you. Behave yourself.

161
00:09:29,458 --> 00:09:30,750
[music stops]

162
00:09:30,833 --> 00:09:33,500
[Felipe's mom] <i>Tidy your room</i>
<i>and get the bed ready for him.</i>

163
00:09:33,583 --> 00:09:36,666
You invited him. Tidy up your own room.
He's not staying in my room.

164
00:09:36,750 --> 00:09:39,083
-Lord help us all.
-[Caio] I'll sleep on the couch.

165
00:09:42,416 --> 00:09:44,958
[gentle guitar music playing]

166
00:09:45,041 --> 00:09:46,958
-Sorry, pal.
-[Felipe] Let me through.

167
00:09:47,041 --> 00:09:49,958
-Let me through, Mom. Thank you. Finally.
-Fine. Go!

168
00:09:51,375 --> 00:09:52,708
[Caio] Hey.

169
00:09:52,791 --> 00:09:54,458
What's the Wi-Fi password?

170
00:09:54,541 --> 00:09:58,416
Merylstreep1979.
She won her first Oscar that year.

171
00:09:58,500 --> 00:10:00,416
Uh… How do you spell Meryl Streep?

172
00:10:05,666 --> 00:10:08,125
DAY 1

173
00:10:08,208 --> 00:10:10,375
[screams and grunts]

174
00:10:10,458 --> 00:10:11,541
[alert on cell phone]

175
00:10:11,625 --> 00:10:17,125
OLIVIA, I REALLY GOTTA TALK TO YOU.
WHEN CAN YOU SEE ME?

176
00:10:18,458 --> 00:10:20,500
[door opens and closes]

177
00:10:20,583 --> 00:10:22,250
SURE, FELIPE. WHAT TIME CAN YOU…

178
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:25,500
My mom brought a guy into the house.

179
00:10:25,583 --> 00:10:27,833
-Good afternoon, Felipe.
-Good afternoon.

180
00:10:27,916 --> 00:10:30,208
Sorry, I couldn't wait
for our next appointment.

181
00:10:30,291 --> 00:10:32,291
Your mother obviously
has the right to date.

182
00:10:32,375 --> 00:10:34,000
That was something we discussed.

183
00:10:34,083 --> 00:10:37,416
Not like this though, Olivia. It's the
neighbor's son. He's staying for 15 days.

184
00:10:37,500 --> 00:10:41,708
Do you know what it's like to be stuck
for 15 days in your house with a stranger?

185
00:10:41,791 --> 00:10:43,166
Anything worse than that?

186
00:10:43,250 --> 00:10:46,708
After 20 years as a psychologist,
I can assure you yes, there is.

187
00:10:46,791 --> 00:10:50,041
I won't survive this.
If I die, I'm gonna blame you.

188
00:10:50,125 --> 00:10:51,416
You're not gonna die.

189
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:54,083
And you need to learn
a little more about boundaries.

190
00:10:54,666 --> 00:10:56,750
We'll talk about it
at your next appointment.

191
00:10:57,458 --> 00:10:59,958
No one in the world has it worse than me.

192
00:11:00,041 --> 00:11:02,583
[tense music playing]

193
00:11:03,750 --> 00:11:04,958
[music becomes ominous]

194
00:11:05,041 --> 00:11:07,125
The victim's body looked like a sieve.

195
00:11:07,875 --> 00:11:10,041
-Looks like we're dealing with a monster.
-Exactly.

196
00:11:10,125 --> 00:11:13,500
And that's why I'm gonna be
assigning you a new partner.

197
00:11:14,791 --> 00:11:15,875
[Felipe] A partner?

198
00:11:15,958 --> 00:11:19,458
-I'm sorry, but I work much better alone.
-I know.

199
00:11:19,541 --> 00:11:22,625
He's only gonna end up
slowing me down. It's a terrible idea.

200
00:11:22,708 --> 00:11:25,291
-What're you trying to say?
-Exactly what you think I'm saying.

201
00:11:25,375 --> 00:11:27,708
All right, enough.
You don't have a choice.

202
00:11:28,666 --> 00:11:30,291
From now on, you two--

203
00:11:30,375 --> 00:11:32,416
-[audio distortion]
-[music stops]

204
00:11:37,125 --> 00:11:39,708
-[Caio] That's it. Okay.
-[player] <i>Copy that. I'll follow you.</i>

205
00:11:39,791 --> 00:11:43,500
-[character] <i>Bomb has been planted.</i>
-Nah, you got this. I'll meet you there.

206
00:11:43,583 --> 00:11:45,416
-[character] <i>Go! Go! Go!</i>
-Hold on.

207
00:11:46,208 --> 00:11:47,333
You need something?

208
00:11:47,416 --> 00:11:49,666
Wi-Fi is slow.
Think you could pause that?

209
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:52,458
[chuckles] No, that's not my dad, no.

210
00:11:52,541 --> 00:11:54,291
Game's live so I can't pause it.

211
00:11:54,375 --> 00:11:55,750
You can wait a minute.

212
00:11:55,833 --> 00:11:58,458
-[video game explosion]
-No, don't be dumb. You can't go alone.

213
00:11:58,541 --> 00:11:59,666
Wait. I'm coming.

214
00:11:59,750 --> 00:12:03,166
-[player] <i>Where you at?</i>
-Calm down! I'm coming. No, don't go in!

215
00:12:03,250 --> 00:12:05,166
-No!
-[player chatters]

216
00:12:05,250 --> 00:12:06,458
[electronic chime]

217
00:12:06,541 --> 00:12:09,000
[intriguing music playing]

218
00:12:11,666 --> 00:12:12,791
Sweet dreams.

