[Rita] All right, now!

461
00:27:07,125 --> 00:27:10,500
Come here. I want you with Felipe,
he's a good dancer.

462
00:27:10,583 --> 00:27:12,083
Show him the way.

463
00:27:12,583 --> 00:27:14,750
Five, six, seven, eight.

464
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:21,500
Step back. And then forward.

465
00:27:21,583 --> 00:27:24,291
-[woman] …three, five, six…
-That's it.

466
00:27:24,375 --> 00:27:27,875
Your left leg forward first,
and then the right one.

467
00:27:28,458 --> 00:27:31,375
Four, five, six and six, seven.

468
00:27:32,583 --> 00:27:34,416
And then you repeat the step. See?

469
00:27:39,625 --> 00:27:42,375
[moody music playing]

470
00:27:47,375 --> 00:27:48,875
I'm getting the hang of it.

471
00:27:51,125 --> 00:27:52,666
[Rita] There, that's it!

472
00:27:52,750 --> 00:27:54,125
Good!

473
00:28:10,083 --> 00:28:11,833
One, two, three.

474
00:28:11,916 --> 00:28:13,958
-Dudu, the fatso!
-He's a lardass.

475
00:28:14,041 --> 00:28:17,208
-Hey! Look, guys, he's gonna cry!
-[boy 1] Of course he's gonna cry!

476
00:28:17,291 --> 00:28:20,291
Don't tell me you're gonna cry!
I bet you will.

477
00:28:20,375 --> 00:28:22,041
Why don't you cry to your mommy?

478
00:28:22,125 --> 00:28:24,916
[overlapping chatter]

479
00:28:26,333 --> 00:28:29,416
-What do you think you're doing?
-[kids] Huh? Nothing at all, sir.

480
00:28:29,500 --> 00:28:32,166
-[Felipe] Get out of here!
-[child] Run! Go! Hurry!

481
00:28:32,250 --> 00:28:34,291
[overlapping shouting]

482
00:28:36,375 --> 00:28:37,458
Are you okay?

483
00:28:38,416 --> 00:28:40,291
Don't worry, I'm here now.

484
00:28:41,375 --> 00:28:42,375
Thank you.

485
00:28:47,958 --> 00:28:49,958
That's good. You drew that?

486
00:28:50,750 --> 00:28:53,166
I drew that last week
in Miss Rita's classroom.

487
00:28:53,250 --> 00:28:54,666
I know her well.

488
00:28:55,375 --> 00:28:56,750
She's a really good teacher.

489
00:28:56,833 --> 00:28:59,166
She's crazy, too.
But that's why I like her.

490
00:28:59,750 --> 00:29:02,791
I agree with you.
But don't tell her I said so.

491
00:29:10,458 --> 00:29:12,666
Those idiots are always gonna pick on you.

492
00:29:13,666 --> 00:29:15,708
Best thing you can do, I say,

493
00:29:16,208 --> 00:29:17,833
just stay away from them.

494
00:29:17,916 --> 00:29:21,083
Just go do something happy instead.
You can always draw.

495
00:29:21,166 --> 00:29:25,083
That is the worst advice ever.
Running from a problem doesn't solve it.

496
00:29:25,166 --> 00:29:26,958
He needs real advice right now.

497
00:29:27,541 --> 00:29:29,458
I can tell you that Batman wouldn't run.

498
00:29:29,541 --> 00:29:32,625
And next he'll tell you
that Batman's a billionaire, you know?

499
00:29:33,166 --> 00:29:35,666
Come with me.
I'll give you advice you can use.

500
00:29:38,708 --> 00:29:40,041
Come on, guys.

501
00:29:40,125 --> 00:29:43,416
[rock music playing]

502
00:29:56,833 --> 00:29:59,541
You realize you're just teaching him
how to lose faster?

503
00:29:59,625 --> 00:30:02,375
-Caio, I'm a walking target.
-Relax.

504
00:30:02,458 --> 00:30:04,083
I've got you, okay?

505
00:30:05,208 --> 00:30:06,416
All right guys, come on.

506
00:30:06,500 --> 00:30:07,875
You're mine now. Let's go.

507
00:30:09,375 --> 00:30:12,375
-[man] All right! Let's go.
-[Caio] Come back this way, stay here.

508
00:30:12,458 --> 00:30:13,416
[man] Line up!

509
00:30:14,583 --> 00:30:16,375
-Let's play!
-[blows whistle]

510
00:30:16,458 --> 00:30:18,833
[children shouting]

511
00:30:22,250 --> 00:30:24,708
-Get back, Get back!
-[man] Go!

512
00:30:32,750 --> 00:30:34,333
That guy is killing us!

513
00:30:56,708 --> 00:30:57,708
Go.

514
00:30:59,416 --> 00:31:01,583
You got this! Go, go, go go go!

515
00:31:06,375 --> 00:31:08,333
[rock music ends]

516
00:31:08,416 --> 00:31:09,750
GG!

517
00:31:09,833 --> 00:31:11,041
What'd you just call me?

518
00:31:11,791 --> 00:31:14,125
Uh… GG is "good game."

519
00:31:14,208 --> 00:31:16,583
You say it to each other
when you're online.

520
00:31:16,666 --> 00:31:19,333
Uh, we should go
before child services gets here.

521
00:31:19,416 --> 00:31:20,416
[Caio chuckles]

522
00:31:20,500 --> 00:31:22,708
-I'll have to talk to Marcela.
-I'm going home.

523
00:31:22,791 --> 00:31:24,958
-Goodbye, sweetheart. Love you.
-See you, Mom.

524
00:31:25,041 --> 00:31:27,000
-Okay. Bye, Angela.
-See you later, Rita.

525
00:31:27,500 --> 00:31:28,583
See you later.

526
00:31:31,333 --> 00:31:33,250
Hey, wait!

527
00:31:36,083 --> 00:31:37,625
This is for you guys.

528
00:31:38,791 --> 00:31:41,583
-Well, thank you, Dudu.
-[Caio] It's beautiful.

529
00:31:42,291 --> 00:31:44,083
I'll keep it forever, okay?

530
00:31:45,458 --> 00:31:46,375
See you, Dudu.

531
00:31:46,458 --> 00:31:47,875
-Thank you.
-See you later.

532
00:31:49,500 --> 00:31:51,375
Ah, I see he got my curls, too.

533
00:31:57,166 --> 00:31:59,791
[quiet guitar music playing]

534
00:31:59,875 --> 00:32:00,875
[chuckles]

535
00:32:03,541 --> 00:32:04,500
[bones crack]

536
00:32:05,541 --> 00:32:07,375
[Caio] <i>Oh, poor thing, he's in pain!</i>

537
00:32:07,458 --> 00:32:08,916
[lively action music playing]

538
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:11,500
<i>That's his problem.</i>
<i>He shouldn't have been so annoying.</i>

539
00:32:11,583 --> 00:32:15,500
<i>You could offer him a comfortable bed,</i>
<i>though. He was so great today.</i>

540
00:32:15,583 --> 00:32:17,750
[Felipe] <i>Oh, so it's okay</i>
<i>for us to hit kids now?</i>

541
00:32:17,833 --> 00:32:20,750
<i>If that's the case,</i>
<i>I should stay with the Joker.</i>

542
00:32:21,708 --> 00:32:23,000
Stop talking!

543
00:32:23,083 --> 00:32:24,875
[pop music playing faintly]

544
00:32:24,958 --> 00:32:25,958
Didn't say anything.

545
00:32:29,083 --> 00:32:30,958
Sorry, I was daydreaming.

546
00:32:31,041 --> 00:32:32,125
[chuckles]

547
00:32:37,416 --> 00:32:38,666
Want to sleep in my room?

548
00:32:38,750 --> 00:32:40,166
-Just because…
-Yes.

549
00:32:40,250 --> 00:32:42,083
…I know sleeping on the couch is awful.

550
00:32:42,166 --> 00:32:43,208
Thank you.

551
00:32:47,916 --> 00:32:50,291
It was really great
what you did for that kid.

552
00:32:51,333 --> 00:32:53,625
Those little idiots had to learn a lesson.

553
00:32:54,583 --> 00:32:58,791
I just know nailing those kids with a ball
was the coolest thing that he's ever done.

554
00:32:58,875 --> 00:33:00,041
[Caio chuckles]

555
00:33:00,875 --> 00:33:05,000
Yeah. It's really hard
not having friends at that age.

556
00:33:07,458 --> 00:33:09,791
[contemplative music playing]

557
00:33:13,250 --> 00:33:15,333
Why'd you disappear, Felipe?

558
00:33:15,416 --> 00:33:16,750
I didn't disappear.

559
00:33:18,750 --> 00:33:21,875
On the contrary, I'd say I've been
getting harder to miss every day.

560
00:33:21,958 --> 00:33:23,125
[chuckles]

561
00:33:23,708 --> 00:33:25,708
I… was really upset that you

562
00:33:26,583 --> 00:33:29,000
<i>suddenly stopped going to the pool.</i>

563
00:33:29,083 --> 00:33:31,916
<i>Then, you grew up and got all… quiet.</i>

564
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:35,125
And I didn't know
if you were shy, or just a jerk.

565
00:33:36,250 --> 00:33:38,625
But now that I'm here,
it's pretty obvious.

566
00:33:38,708 --> 00:33:39,958
You're definitely a jerk.

567
00:33:40,041 --> 00:33:41,125
[mock gasp]

568
00:33:41,666 --> 00:33:44,583
Oh, I was gonna say
the same thing about you, though, Caio.

569
00:33:44,666 --> 00:33:48,708
[chuckles] But after today, I guess
I would say… You're 50% of a jerk.

570
00:33:48,791 --> 00:33:49,958
[mock gasp]

571
00:33:52,166 --> 00:33:54,333
Weren't there stars on the ceiling before?

572
00:33:54,958 --> 00:33:59,208
Oh, no, they're still there. It's just
that as time goes by they fade, you know?

573
00:33:59,291 --> 00:34:03,250
I remember I tried to get my mom to buy
me some, but she wouldn't let me get any.

574
00:34:03,333 --> 00:34:05,000
They're really hard to take off.

575
00:34:05,083 --> 00:34:08,166
I know. Those stickers
I stuck on my window are still there.

576
00:34:08,250 --> 00:34:10,166
The ones with <i>Mulan</i>?

577
00:34:10,250 --> 00:34:13,041
Ah, don't judge.
I always had a huge crush on her.

578
00:34:13,125 --> 00:34:16,333
It was the only one she allowed.
Of my decorations.

579
00:34:16,416 --> 00:34:18,583
She's still old fashioned
about that stuff.

580
00:34:18,666 --> 00:34:21,500
It's impossible to talk to Caio.
It just doesn't work.

581
00:34:21,583 --> 00:34:24,750
But I thought you said he
spent the whole night talking to you.

582
00:34:24,833 --> 00:34:27,041
Yeah. But this morning…

583
00:34:27,125 --> 00:34:30,000
-Felipe, you heard the new Gaga song?
-[electronic music playing]

584
00:34:30,083 --> 00:34:32,833
Uh-huh.
[in voiceover] <i>Of course I heard it, Caio.</i>

585
00:34:32,916 --> 00:34:35,458
When the greatest artist ever
to walk the face of the Earth

586
00:34:35,541 --> 00:34:38,583
releases new music,
you listen to it the second it comes out.

587
00:34:38,666 --> 00:34:40,833
You don't stop listening
until the next day.

588
00:34:40,916 --> 00:34:43,500
[electronic music continues]

589
00:34:43,583 --> 00:34:45,250
[music stops]

590
00:34:45,333 --> 00:34:48,250
Uh, Lady Gaga is super famous.
Know who she is?

591
00:34:48,333 --> 00:34:50,000
I do know Lady Gaga.

592
00:34:50,083 --> 00:34:53,541
I'm sorry, I just I don't know
what the older generations are into.

593
00:34:54,500 --> 00:34:57,791
Generations? Just how old
do you think that I am?

594
00:34:57,875 --> 00:35:00,833
Uh… How about we get back to the therapy?

595
00:35:00,916 --> 00:35:04,250
Is it possible he knew that your love
for Gaga was a little extreme?

596
00:35:04,333 --> 00:35:06,916
It could be Caio using it
to start a conversation.

597
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:08,958
That would be so much easier at night.

598
00:35:09,041 --> 00:35:10,041
It would?

599
00:35:10,125 --> 00:35:11,500
But why?

600
00:35:11,583 --> 00:35:13,250
[gentle guitar music playing]

601
00:35:13,333 --> 00:35:14,875
'Cause no one can see you.

602
00:35:16,041 --> 00:35:17,875
All right, here's your homework.

603
00:35:17,958 --> 00:35:21,416
I want you to start a conversation
with Caio during the day.

604
00:35:24,208 --> 00:35:27,166
I'm on vacation, Olivia.
You're assigning homework?

605
00:35:28,625 --> 00:35:30,625
[music stops]

606
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:36,708
-Hey.
-[man] How's it going, Lipe?

607
00:35:36,791 --> 00:35:38,000
You need anything?

608
00:35:38,083 --> 00:35:40,583
-Nah, I'm just having a quick look.
-Sounds good.

609
00:35:40,666 --> 00:35:43,250
["Idiota" by Jão playing]

610
00:35:50,458 --> 00:35:51,666
Just this.

611
00:35:51,750 --> 00:35:53,041
-That it today?
-Yeah.

612
00:35:53,125 --> 00:35:55,666
-Is this for you or someone else?
-It's a gift.

613
00:35:55,750 --> 00:35:57,625
-How much is it? Ah.
-Only 18.

614
00:35:58,208 --> 00:36:00,000
-Here you go.
-All right, thank you.

615
00:36:00,083 --> 00:36:01,291
He's gonna like it.

616
00:36:01,375 --> 00:36:03,500
[lyrics in Portuguese]

617
00:36:20,583 --> 00:36:22,333
-Hi, Francisco.
-I read that one.

618
00:36:22,416 --> 00:36:23,833
I really liked it. Good stuff.

619
00:36:23,916 --> 00:36:25,750
Ah, it's not for me, it's a present.

620
00:36:25,833 --> 00:36:28,875
Let me know if you ever want
recommendations for fantasy or sci-fi.

621
00:36:28,958 --> 00:36:30,125
Well, thank you.

622
00:36:30,625 --> 00:36:32,333
Have you by any chance seen Caio?

623
00:36:32,416 --> 00:36:34,916
Oh, Caio came down here earlier,
but he went out.

624
00:36:35,000 --> 00:36:36,625
Ok, thanks. See ya.

625
00:36:36,708 --> 00:36:38,958
["Idiota" continues]

626
00:36:58,333 --> 00:37:00,250
-Hey.
-Hi.

627
00:37:01,125 --> 00:37:04,833
DAY 5

628
00:37:04,916 --> 00:37:06,666
["Idiota" stops]

629
00:37:06,750 --> 00:37:08,083
That yours?

630
00:37:09,875 --> 00:37:12,000
Ah, no, I bought it for you.
It's a present.

631
00:37:14,666 --> 00:37:16,625
It's just a little gift,
so don't freak out.

632
00:37:17,416 --> 00:37:20,625
I was going through a second-hand
bookstore and had to get it for you.

633
00:37:20,708 --> 00:37:22,666
-It was on sale.
-No, I'll read it.

634
00:37:23,166 --> 00:37:26,458
Although there's no point,
since I know Gandalf dies in the end now.

635
00:37:26,541 --> 00:37:29,416
[chuckles] I shouldn't
have told you that, I'm sorry.

636
00:37:32,250 --> 00:37:34,416
Going to the movies tomorrow.
You wanna come?

637
00:37:34,500 --> 00:37:36,708
[whimsical music playing]

638
00:37:36,791 --> 00:37:38,791
Um, I would. I already have plans though.

639
00:37:38,875 --> 00:37:40,625
During your vacation?

640
00:37:41,625 --> 00:37:43,083
Yeah.

641
00:37:43,166 --> 00:37:46,250
-That's cool. Well, thanks again.
-[door opens]

642
00:37:52,708 --> 00:37:53,916
I'll go with you.

643
00:37:55,000 --> 00:37:56,125
What about your plans?

644
00:37:56,208 --> 00:37:59,375
Well, I'll talk to my secretary
and have her clear my schedule.

645
00:38:01,458 --> 00:38:04,083
That's cool.
Beca's really going to love you.

646
00:38:07,083 --> 00:38:08,333
[Felipe] <i>Beca?</i>

647
00:38:08,416 --> 00:38:11,291
<i>Of course Caio wouldn't invite me</i>
<i>to go to the movies alone.</i>

648
00:38:11,375 --> 00:38:14,125
<i>What was I thinking?</i>
<i>Obviously, there's a girl.</i>

649
00:38:15,500 --> 00:38:17,333
<i>And what's with that name? Beca?</i>

650
00:38:17,416 --> 00:38:20,541
<i>It sounds like a cheerleader</i>
<i>on some show about high school.</i>

651
00:38:20,625 --> 00:38:22,791
IN LOVE IN HIGH SCHOOL

652
00:38:22,875 --> 00:38:26,583
<i>You're just jealous because</i>
<i>Caio likes me more than you.</i>

653
00:38:27,625 --> 00:38:29,583
Shut your mouth, Beca!

654
00:38:29,666 --> 00:38:31,250
[buzzer rings]

655
00:38:32,916 --> 00:38:36,083
Honestly, you'll love Beca.
She's the best person in the world.

656
00:38:36,166 --> 00:38:39,125
-What will we have to talk about, Caio?
-Relax.

657
00:38:40,208 --> 00:38:41,208
There she is.

658
00:38:41,291 --> 00:38:44,500
[upbeat music playing]

659
00:38:47,250 --> 00:38:48,708
Hi. Just a second.

660
00:38:49,250 --> 00:38:51,375
[Felipe] <i>Guys, this is Beca!</i>

661
00:38:53,666 --> 00:38:55,291
[groans] Thank God you're here.

662
00:38:55,375 --> 00:38:58,208
I couldn't take it anymore. I quit, okay?

663
00:38:58,291 --> 00:39:00,833
[chuckles] Just kidding, Robson.
I'm back tomorrow.

664
00:39:01,750 --> 00:39:02,750
This is Beca.

665
00:39:03,250 --> 00:39:05,750
-Hey there.
-Nice to meet you. Felipe.

666
00:39:05,833 --> 00:39:09,166
The famous Felipe.
He talks about you, you know?

667
00:39:09,250 --> 00:39:11,250
You finally found some time for me, huh?

668
00:39:11,333 --> 00:39:14,166
Felipe, some people,
they disappear off to college,

669
00:39:14,250 --> 00:39:16,791
and start working,
and dating, and forget about you.

670
00:39:16,875 --> 00:39:19,208
-Oh, here comes the sermon. Mm.
-Mm.

671
00:39:20,416 --> 00:39:22,791
-Do you have the tickets?
-[Beca] I do.

672
00:39:23,833 --> 00:39:25,291
Have a good one.

673
00:39:26,666 --> 00:39:27,666
Tell me something.

674
00:39:27,750 --> 00:39:31,583
What's it like having to share a house
with this one? [chuckles]

675
00:39:31,666 --> 00:39:34,791
Ever stub your toe on the corner
of the bed? Or had a root canal?

676
00:39:34,875 --> 00:39:36,666
Or a bad kidney stone?

677
00:39:37,916 --> 00:39:39,333
I like him already.

678
00:39:40,833 --> 00:39:46,250
{\an8}DAY 6

679
00:39:46,333 --> 00:39:48,708
["To Know the Odds"
by Bárbara Eugênia playing]

680
00:39:48,791 --> 00:39:51,708
[indistinct chatter]

681
00:39:51,791 --> 00:39:56,291
<i>♪ Like drifting memories</i>
<i>That I might live ♪</i>

682
00:39:57,541 --> 00:40:00,166
[indistinct chatter]

683
00:40:01,500 --> 00:40:03,500
♪ <i>What we’re doing now </i>♪

684
00:40:03,583 --> 00:40:06,750
♪ <i>Apart from being so lost </i>♪

685
00:40:09,041 --> 00:40:11,541
♪ <i>'Cause I’d like to know the odds </i>♪

686
00:40:11,625 --> 00:40:15,750
♪ <i>Like to know the way</i>
<i>It comes down to this </i>♪

687
00:40:15,833 --> 00:40:17,958
-[loud noise in movie]
-[gasps and screams]

688
00:40:18,041 --> 00:40:20,791
♪ <i>Like the way it was </i>♪

689
00:40:20,875 --> 00:40:24,541
♪ <i>Like the way</i>
<i>Way we were used to be </i>♪

690
00:40:24,625 --> 00:40:26,333
That was way better than part two.

691
00:40:26,416 --> 00:40:29,750
The scene where the monster came out
of the screen was better than the sequel.

692
00:40:29,833 --> 00:40:31,666
-Yeah.
-Did you guys like that scene?

693
00:40:31,750 --> 00:40:32,625
Yeah.

694
00:40:32,708 --> 00:40:35,916
Caio doesn't appreciate the beauty
of an exploding head. [chuckles]

695
00:40:36,000 --> 00:40:38,166
What are your favorite scenes from horror?

696
00:40:38,250 --> 00:40:40,291
-Hold on. Uh…
-The <i>Hereditary </i>telephone.

697
00:40:40,375 --> 00:40:43,500
-I loved that one! Yeah.
-Opening scene from <i>Scream</i>, of course.

698
00:40:43,583 --> 00:40:46,458
-And the graduation scene from <i>Carrie</i>!
<i>-Carrie! </i>Oh, yeah!

699
00:40:46,541 --> 00:40:49,416
[Felipe] I am terrified of parties
'cause of that movie.

700
00:40:49,500 --> 00:40:52,458
I'm always waiting for someone
to just pour blood on me.

701
00:40:52,541 --> 00:40:54,000
This would look good on you.

702
00:40:55,000 --> 00:40:57,458
Yeah, well maybe
if there was a bigger size.

703
00:40:57,541 --> 00:40:59,666
["To Know the Odds" continues faintly]

704
00:41:02,125 --> 00:41:04,208
Have you and Caio
known each other a long time?

705
00:41:04,291 --> 00:41:07,583
Ah… He came to my school
in the eighth grade.

706
00:41:07,666 --> 00:41:09,916
We were pretty much
instant friends, you know?

707
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:13,000
There were no other gays
at our school then. [chuckles]

708
00:41:13,083 --> 00:41:14,541
What do you mean, other gays?

709
00:41:14,625 --> 00:41:17,750
Yeah, other than Caio, I think
there were only three other gays there.

710
00:41:17,833 --> 00:41:20,541
-But Caio's not gay.
-What do you mean, Felipe?

711
00:41:20,625 --> 00:41:21,916
Didn't you know?

712
00:41:22,000 --> 00:41:23,916
There's no way he's gay. Look at him.

713
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:26,583
No, Caio isn't gay,
because Caio likes football.

714
00:41:26,666 --> 00:41:28,416
And likes to shoot Orcs.

715
00:41:28,500 --> 00:41:32,083
Last week when Cher came up,
I had to explain who Cher was.

716
00:41:32,166 --> 00:41:34,791
-What gay doesn't know who Cher is?
-Who is that?

717
00:41:34,875 --> 00:41:38,166
-Oh, my love, you're beyond help, honey.
-[chuckles]

718
00:41:38,250 --> 00:41:40,291
Caio's not gay, no way. I'd have known.

719
00:41:40,375 --> 00:41:42,500
There's no gay guys who like those things?

720
00:41:42,583 --> 00:41:45,958
Felipe, gay people can be into all sorts
of things that are macho.

721
00:41:46,041 --> 00:41:47,666
They can even be a serial killer.

722
00:41:47,750 --> 00:41:48,958
Mm.

723
00:41:53,541 --> 00:41:55,375
["To Know the Odds" ends]

724
00:41:55,458 --> 00:41:58,041
Um, guys, what's Musical Wednesdays?

725
00:41:58,125 --> 00:42:01,666
Well, it's Wednesday and we're watching
a musical, it's self-explanatory.

726
00:42:01,750 --> 00:42:04,333
And since it's your first time,
you get to choose.

727
00:42:05,333 --> 00:42:07,166
I'll pass. I don't like musicals.

728
00:42:07,250 --> 00:42:08,708
-[gasps]
-[Felipe] I'm shocked.

729
00:42:08,791 --> 00:42:10,208
-My god.
-[Felipe] Dear lord.

730
00:42:10,291 --> 00:42:12,916
-Oh, I don't feel well.
-Try to breathe, Mom.

731
00:42:13,000 --> 00:42:15,500
Caio, in this house,
you can't say stuff like that.

732
00:42:15,583 --> 00:42:17,500
In reality, no one goes around singing.

733
00:42:17,583 --> 00:42:19,291
-No.
-Of course they sing.

734
00:42:19,375 --> 00:42:21,958
They sing so they can
let all of their feelings out.

735
00:42:22,041 --> 00:42:24,083
Not everything has to make sense.

736
00:42:24,166 --> 00:42:25,833
Forget it, you won't understand.

737
00:42:37,458 --> 00:42:38,541
Um, this.

738
00:42:42,166 --> 00:42:43,250
[Rita] Hm.

739
00:42:43,791 --> 00:42:46,333
[video player door closes]

740
00:42:46,416 --> 00:42:49,416
[upbeat guitar music playing]

741
00:42:52,208 --> 00:42:53,500
[music stops]

742
00:42:54,416 --> 00:42:58,166
["Good Morning Baltimore"
by Bel Moreira & Miguel Lallo playing]

743
00:43:01,541 --> 00:43:03,625
[Felipe] <i>Of course he chose this movie.</i>

744
00:43:03,708 --> 00:43:06,416
<i>It's about a fat girl</i>
<i>who's in love with a pretty boy.</i>

745
00:43:06,500 --> 00:43:08,708
<i>I mean, why be subtle, right?</i>

746
00:43:08,791 --> 00:43:11,291
<i>Beca could not have gotten it more wrong.</i>

747
00:43:11,375 --> 00:43:13,916
<i>What kind of gay doesn't like musicals?</i>

748
00:43:16,208 --> 00:43:19,833
<i>Except when the hot guy came on screen…</i>

749
00:43:20,500 --> 00:43:22,416
<i>It was totally obvious.</i>

750
00:43:22,500 --> 00:43:24,750
[dramatic suspenseful music playing]

751
00:43:26,208 --> 00:43:28,750
[music builds to a climax]

752
00:43:28,833 --> 00:43:30,208
[music stops]

753
00:43:31,125 --> 00:43:33,083
<i>Caio is gay!</i>

754
00:43:33,166 --> 00:43:36,250
<i>Well, Now that I think about it,</i>
<i>it's obvious Caio's gay!</i>

755
00:43:36,333 --> 00:43:37,750
<i>All the signs were there.</i>

756
00:43:37,833 --> 00:43:40,375
<i>Lady Gaga. His love for Dodgeball.</i>

757
00:43:40,458 --> 00:43:42,166
<i>His crush on Mulan?</i>

758
00:43:42,250 --> 00:43:44,333
<i>Oh, and those cute little sailor pajamas…</i>

759
00:43:44,416 --> 00:43:48,875
<i>Sorry to bring up the pajamas again,</i>
<i>but I cannot get them out of my head.</i>

760
00:43:48,958 --> 00:43:51,541
[lively funky music playing]

761
00:43:51,625 --> 00:43:53,375
-[exhales]
-[music stops]

762
00:43:53,458 --> 00:43:55,000
[women chattering]

763
00:43:55,083 --> 00:43:57,500
[Felipe] I'm sorry,
but this is more important.

764
00:43:57,583 --> 00:44:00,916
-[woman] But my dog just died.
-[Felipe] Caio's gay! Caio is gay!

765
00:44:01,000 --> 00:44:03,500
-Caio is gay!
-[Olivia] We'll see each other next week.

766
00:44:03,583 --> 00:44:04,583
DAY 7

767
00:44:04,666 --> 00:44:07,333
[Felipe] This changes everything.
I was getting used to the idea

768
00:44:07,416 --> 00:44:09,208
of sharing a room with him, but now…

769
00:44:09,291 --> 00:44:11,666
Are you going to treat him differently
because he's gay?

770
00:44:13,458 --> 00:44:16,000
Well, you make it sound
like I'm homophobic.

771
00:44:16,708 --> 00:44:19,208
If the only problem now
is that you have a crush--

772
00:44:19,291 --> 00:44:23,375
No, stop, stop. First of all, it's weird
hearing you talk like a teenager.

773
00:44:23,458 --> 00:44:26,458
Secondly, I feel nothing for Caio.
Nothing nothing nothing. You know?

774
00:44:26,541 --> 00:44:28,875
No, not at all. Of course not.

775
00:44:28,958 --> 00:44:31,583
If that's true,
how would his orientation change anything?

776
00:44:31,666 --> 00:44:34,291
[whimsical music playing]

777
00:44:38,041 --> 00:44:42,375
Felipe, if Caio didn't tell you before,
he may have had a reason not to.

778
00:44:46,666 --> 00:44:48,875
Of course he had a reason not to.

779
00:44:48,958 --> 00:44:50,291
I already know that.

780
00:44:51,083 --> 00:44:55,916
[thinking] <i>He didn't tell me</i>
<i>that he was gay because I am fat.</i>

781
00:44:58,625 --> 00:44:59,916
<i>I've been stalking Caio.</i>

782
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:03,375
<i>And in just the past week,</i>
<i>he's already liked 57 photos of boys.</i>

783
00:45:03,458 --> 00:45:06,291
<i>I'll give you a prize if you guess</i>
<i>what they all had in common.</i>

784
00:45:06,375 --> 00:45:10,125
<i>That's right, skinny. They're all skinny.</i>

785
00:45:10,208 --> 00:45:13,666
<i>And that… brings me to him. Denis.</i>

786
00:45:13,750 --> 00:45:17,250
<i>The boy Caio has liked the most</i>
<i>in the past month, my new arch-enemy.</i>

787
00:45:17,333 --> 00:45:20,500
<i>That is, if I had a crush on Caio.</i>
<i>Everyone knows I obviously don't.</i>

788
00:45:20,583 --> 00:45:25,416
<i>All-Soup diet, the ice cube diet,</i>
<i>Ozempic, bariatric surgery…</i>

789
00:45:25,500 --> 00:45:28,916
<i>How am I gonna lose 30 pounds</i>
<i>in two weeks?</i>

790
00:45:29,000 --> 00:45:30,541
<i>I need to make a change.</i>

791
00:45:31,125 --> 00:45:33,500
<i>Not just for Caio, but for my own health.</i>

792
00:45:33,583 --> 00:45:35,250
LOSE WEIGHT QUICK!
RESULTS GUARANTEED

793
00:45:35,333 --> 00:45:36,583
<i>I can't keep being me.</i>

794
00:45:37,625 --> 00:45:39,375
[music stops]

795
00:45:41,875 --> 00:45:42,916
[phone rings]

796
00:45:44,791 --> 00:45:46,041
[doctor] Hm.

797
00:45:49,083 --> 00:45:50,333
[watch beeps]

798
00:45:51,041 --> 00:45:52,250
Mmmm.

799
00:45:53,000 --> 00:45:54,875
Get this… [groans]

800
00:45:55,875 --> 00:45:58,583
You say you wanna lose a few pounds, yes?

801
00:45:58,666 --> 00:46:01,291
-Mm. A lot more than a few.
-I see.

802
00:46:02,416 --> 00:46:05,333
Nowadays, there are
a lot of options for cases like yours.

803
00:46:06,000 --> 00:46:07,791
Can you give me the fastest one?

804
00:46:07,875 --> 00:46:10,083
Oh. The fastest one?

805
00:46:10,666 --> 00:46:11,583
Oh.

806
00:46:11,666 --> 00:46:14,041
[jazzy music playing]

807
00:46:16,583 --> 00:46:19,500
Let's start by cutting all your fat off!

808
00:46:19,583 --> 00:46:24,125
[both screaming]

809
00:46:24,208 --> 00:46:25,666
[music stops]

810
00:46:25,750 --> 00:46:27,958
[panting]

811
00:46:36,666 --> 00:46:38,583
-Ah! Jeez, Caio!
-[dramatic musical stinger]

812
00:46:38,666 --> 00:46:41,625
-Why are you sneaking around?
-I'm just getting water.

813
00:46:42,166 --> 00:46:44,583
Yeah, me too.
But this was in the way though.

814
00:46:45,208 --> 00:46:46,250
I see.

815
00:46:50,708 --> 00:46:53,541
[lounge music playing]

816
00:46:54,750 --> 00:46:56,125
[cereal clattering]

817
00:46:56,208 --> 00:46:58,166
DAY 8

818
00:46:58,250 --> 00:47:00,208
What's with the dark circles
under your eyes?

819
00:47:02,333 --> 00:47:04,875
Hey, Rita, are you sure
I can invite the girls?

820
00:47:04,958 --> 00:47:06,875
[Rita] Of course, why wouldn't I be?

821
00:47:07,375 --> 00:47:10,041
Just that they're a couple.
My mom doesn't like it when--

822
00:47:10,125 --> 00:47:12,166
-Lesbians?
-Oh, the horror!

823
00:47:12,250 --> 00:47:13,333
Lesbians?

824
00:47:14,041 --> 00:47:16,916
[chuckling] Of course,
it's not problem at all.

825
00:47:17,500 --> 00:47:19,291
I almost became a lesbian in college.

826
00:47:19,375 --> 00:47:20,541
-[Felipe] Mom!
-[Rita] What?

827
00:47:20,625 --> 00:47:22,166
One kiss doesn't make you one.

828
00:47:22,833 --> 00:47:26,333
-Who said it was just a kiss?
-Lord, I don't wanna hear all the details.

829
00:47:26,416 --> 00:47:28,416
-Please don't.
-I wanna hear the details.

830
00:47:28,500 --> 00:47:31,208
-Then, I'll tell you later. [chuckles]
-[Caio] Well,

831
00:47:31,291 --> 00:47:33,000
the pool's packed, it's reopened.

832
00:47:33,666 --> 00:47:36,958
So, we'll all be down there
if you wanna come find us.

833
00:47:38,041 --> 00:47:40,375
-Thanks again, Rita.
-Bye for now.

834
00:47:40,458 --> 00:47:42,041
[door opens]

835
00:47:45,000 --> 00:47:46,000
[door shuts]

836
00:47:46,875 --> 00:47:49,416
Don't even try,
you know the answer, all right?

837
00:47:49,500 --> 00:47:52,833
-What? I didn't say anything.
-I can hear you think, though.

838
00:47:52,916 --> 00:47:55,541
[upbeat guitar music playing]

839
00:47:58,916 --> 00:48:02,083
I still won't go, but if I did,

840
00:48:02,166 --> 00:48:04,166
where are my swim shorts?

841
00:48:06,375 --> 00:48:09,791
[giggles] Yes! Oh, I don't believe it!

842
00:48:09,875 --> 00:48:11,041
Mom.

843
00:48:11,125 --> 00:48:13,791
-What is wrong with you?
-[blowing air] Oh, it's just…

844
00:48:13,875 --> 00:48:15,375
[water splashing]

845
00:48:15,458 --> 00:48:18,083
[chuckling]

846
00:48:18,166 --> 00:48:20,166
[music stops]

847
00:48:21,583 --> 00:48:23,125
[Beca] Cannonball!

848
00:48:26,375 --> 00:48:28,416
-You don't know how to do it.
-[gasps]

849
00:48:31,083 --> 00:48:34,000
-Where did you get that?
-Oh, some kid left it here.

850
00:48:34,666 --> 00:48:36,750
I offered to look after it. Name's Harry.

851
00:48:36,833 --> 00:48:38,791
-Potter?
-No… Styles.

852
00:48:41,041 --> 00:48:44,250
Hey, guys, the water's amazing.
Are you getting in?

853
00:48:44,333 --> 00:48:45,916
-In a little while.
-In a while.

854
00:48:46,416 --> 00:48:48,000
[Caio] Mmm.

855
00:48:49,416 --> 00:48:51,208
Aren't you getting in, Melissa?

856
00:48:52,250 --> 00:48:56,333
Usually, "In a little while" is universal
code for not wanting to get in the water.

857
00:48:56,416 --> 00:48:58,708
Yeah, I just prefer to stay on the side.

858
00:48:58,791 --> 00:49:01,333
I don't like being in a bikini
in front of everyone.

859
00:49:01,416 --> 00:49:03,416
Really? Someone as thin and hot as you?

860
00:49:03,500 --> 00:49:06,333
Just because I'm thin doesn't mean
I don't have other insecurities.

861
00:49:06,416 --> 00:49:07,708
Well, that is a crime.

862
00:49:10,208 --> 00:49:12,416
Hey, babe! Get in the pool.

863
00:49:13,333 --> 00:49:14,666
I said, in a little while.

864
00:49:14,750 --> 00:49:17,333
I know. That was a little while ago.

865
00:49:17,416 --> 00:49:19,541
-She's worked out the universal code.
-Mm.

866
00:49:19,625 --> 00:49:20,791
[chuckles]

867
00:49:21,708 --> 00:49:24,750
Come have fun with me,
enjoy the pool and get some sun.

868
00:49:25,333 --> 00:49:26,208
Okay?

869
00:49:30,583 --> 00:49:32,875
[upbeat music playing]

870
00:49:38,625 --> 00:49:40,625
[Melissa and Beca squeal]

871
00:49:41,708 --> 00:49:42,875
[Caio] All right!

872
00:49:44,083 --> 00:49:45,083
[Melissa] Hey!

873
00:49:45,583 --> 00:49:46,708
[girls laugh]

874
00:49:49,125 --> 00:49:51,041
[Caio laughs]

875
00:50:14,833 --> 00:50:16,083
-Third wheel.
-[chuckles]

876
00:50:19,458 --> 00:50:21,833
Remember playing mermaids
when we were kids?

877
00:50:29,333 --> 00:50:30,541
Not really, no.

878
00:50:33,916 --> 00:50:35,583
You really don't want to go in?

879
00:50:38,458 --> 00:50:40,333
-In a little while.
-Hm.

880
00:50:41,541 --> 00:50:43,875
Gays, I was just saying to Mel,

881
00:50:44,458 --> 00:50:46,750
we should go
to the Persimmon Festival tomorrow.

882
00:50:46,833 --> 00:50:48,666
-Let's go!
-Yes. Yes.

883
00:50:48,750 --> 00:50:50,416
-No, I can't.
-[Melissa] You can't?

884
00:50:50,500 --> 00:50:51,500
-I can't go.
-Why?

885
00:50:51,583 --> 00:50:54,250
Ever since what happened at the pool,
I'm not allowed to go out.

886
00:50:54,333 --> 00:50:55,750
She told the doorman, so, no.

887
00:50:56,416 --> 00:50:59,083
-It won't work.
-I think we can figure this out.

888
00:50:59,708 --> 00:51:00,583
How?

889
00:51:01,416 --> 00:51:03,708
It is so hot here,
sweetie, I'm telling you.

890
00:51:03,791 --> 00:51:06,916
<i>And you're not gonna go hang out</i>
<i>with those girls, now, right?</i>

891
00:51:07,000 --> 00:51:10,791
Of course not, mom. I'm going to hang up.
Okay? I love you, goodnight.

892
00:51:11,291 --> 00:51:14,000
All right, good night.
I love you… Oh, he's gone already.

893
00:51:14,083 --> 00:51:15,875
[Felipe<i>] First, we trick your mom.</i>

894
00:51:16,833 --> 00:51:18,666
DAY 9

895
00:51:18,750 --> 00:51:21,583
<i>Then we distract mine with a K-drama.</i>

896
00:51:21,666 --> 00:51:24,416
-[indistinct chatter]
-[lively rock music playing]

897
00:51:26,583 --> 00:51:29,416
<i>Francisco watches games on his phone.</i>
<i>There's always a delay.</i>

898
00:51:29,500 --> 00:51:31,500
-[sports announcer chatters]
-Hey, Francisco.

899
00:51:31,583 --> 00:51:34,041
I think my mom left a key here for me.

900
00:51:34,125 --> 00:51:35,583
No, there isn't one.

901
00:51:35,666 --> 00:51:37,666
-She did.
-She didn't leave anything.

902
00:51:37,750 --> 00:51:40,416
-Goal!
-These are the keys here. Nothing here.

903
00:51:40,500 --> 00:51:42,208
[sports announcer chatters]

904
00:51:44,916 --> 00:51:46,333
Oh, damn delay.

905
00:51:46,916 --> 00:51:47,916
Goal!

906
00:51:50,458 --> 00:51:52,000
What? Where's the goal?

907
00:51:54,458 --> 00:51:56,958
Everyone ready?
Hurry up, let's go, let's book it!

908
00:51:57,041 --> 00:51:58,666
27TH PERSIMMON FESTIVAL

909
00:51:58,750 --> 00:52:01,333
-[person] Whoo!
-[Caio] Wait, guys, Hold on, wait.

910
00:52:01,833 --> 00:52:03,333
Your outfit's a little boring.

911
00:52:06,458 --> 00:52:08,458
I bought it at that store the other day.

912
00:52:09,291 --> 00:52:12,791
I went ahead
and asked your mom what size you are.

913
00:52:13,958 --> 00:52:17,500
-Now we're even. Thanks for the book.
-[Melissa] Put it on.

914
00:52:17,583 --> 00:52:18,583
[Caio chuckles]

915
00:52:18,666 --> 00:52:20,750
-Mm, put it on.
-[Felipe] Can you hold this?

916
00:52:20,833 --> 00:52:22,541
-I got you.
-Come here, come here.

917
00:52:23,750 --> 00:52:24,708
Here.

918
00:52:25,541 --> 00:52:27,250
-There you go.
-[Felipe] Thank you.

919
00:52:27,333 --> 00:52:29,958
[lively festive music playing]

920
00:52:41,000 --> 00:52:42,166
You look good.

921
00:52:45,958 --> 00:52:47,375
[Beca] Now, let's go party!

922
00:52:48,291 --> 00:52:50,083
Let's go. Come on!

923
00:52:50,166 --> 00:52:52,208
[Beca and Caio chuckle]

924
00:52:53,750 --> 00:52:55,291
Let's fix you up.

925
00:52:56,833 --> 00:52:58,875
-By the way, I ship him.
-And who?

926
00:52:58,958 --> 00:53:01,875
-You.
-There is no way that's happening.

927
00:53:01,958 --> 00:53:03,791
-Well, let me believe.
-Okay fine.

928
00:53:03,875 --> 00:53:06,958
[man] Welcome, everyone,
to the Persimmon Festival!

929
00:53:07,041 --> 00:53:08,875
[crowd cheers]

930
00:53:08,958 --> 00:53:12,291
<i>Here are the winners of this year's</i>
<i>contest, Mr. and Miss Persimmon:</i>

931
00:53:12,375 --> 00:53:15,083
<i>Jonathan and Jennifer!</i>

932
