Caio and I are totally dating now!

1166
01:10:02,666 --> 01:10:04,166
-Okay, Felipe.
-No.

1167
01:10:04,250 --> 01:10:07,333
First there was an almost kiss
at the Persimmon Festival.

1168
01:10:07,833 --> 01:10:11,333
Then he disappeared and I thought
he wanted nothing to do with me at all.

1169
01:10:11,416 --> 01:10:15,208
Then he took me to a special place
and he said he was upset with his parents.

1170
01:10:15,291 --> 01:10:16,875
And then we just made out.

1171
01:10:17,458 --> 01:10:19,875
Then he wanted to get a tattoo.
So I also got one.

1172
01:10:19,958 --> 01:10:21,250
Does your mom know this?

1173
01:10:21,333 --> 01:10:23,833
-Then I beat up those jerks from school.
-What now?

1174
01:10:23,916 --> 01:10:26,666
And then we took one of those
hurricane trolleys back to his place.

1175
01:10:27,333 --> 01:10:30,041
At first, we were just
holding on to each other.

1176
01:10:30,958 --> 01:10:32,625
Then more.

1177
01:10:32,708 --> 01:10:34,250
[gentle guitar music playing]

1178
01:10:34,333 --> 01:10:35,333
You're beautiful.

1179
01:10:35,916 --> 01:10:37,666
He said I was beautiful.

1180
01:10:40,708 --> 01:10:42,458
How did that make you feel?

1181
01:10:42,541 --> 01:10:43,875
[chuckles] Good.

1182
01:10:43,958 --> 01:10:45,333
It felt great.

1183
01:10:46,333 --> 01:10:49,666
And was it as scary
as you imagined it would be, though?

1184
01:10:49,750 --> 01:10:50,875
No.

1185
01:10:51,500 --> 01:10:53,708
So anyway, basically, we're dating now.

1186
01:10:55,750 --> 01:10:57,833
Have you two talked about that?

1187
01:10:58,666 --> 01:11:00,708
Olivia, don't you want details?

1188
01:11:01,791 --> 01:11:06,208
Jeez, I could never be a psychologist,
Olivia. I would wanna know all the gossip.

1189
01:11:06,291 --> 01:11:07,291
And?

1190
01:11:08,500 --> 01:11:10,375
I've known him since I was a toddler.

1191
01:11:10,458 --> 01:11:13,583
We sleep in the same room.
And we're doing everything together.

1192
01:11:13,666 --> 01:11:15,500
If that's not dating, then what is?

1193
01:11:16,291 --> 01:11:20,750
It makes me very happy
for me to see you so excited.

1194
01:11:20,833 --> 01:11:23,208
It's been quite a while
since I've seen you smile.

1195
01:11:23,291 --> 01:11:24,708
But?

1196
01:11:25,666 --> 01:11:27,041
But…

1197
01:11:27,541 --> 01:11:30,625
You can't just keep living inside
your head, Felipe.

1198
01:11:30,708 --> 01:11:34,500
You can't spend your whole life
avoiding difficult conversations.

1199
01:11:35,000 --> 01:11:38,666
I really think that you need to talk
to him, and tell him how you feel.

1200
01:11:38,750 --> 01:11:40,666
I'm not any good at that though.

1201
01:11:41,375 --> 01:11:43,125
Then… write it.

1202
01:11:44,125 --> 01:11:45,208
What do you mean?

1203
01:11:45,291 --> 01:11:47,583
You spent almost 15 days together, right?

1204
01:11:47,666 --> 01:11:49,375
Well, make a list.

1205
01:11:49,458 --> 01:11:51,208
Fifteen things that you've learned.

1206
01:11:51,291 --> 01:11:53,333
Well that's homework, you know?

1207
01:11:56,500 --> 01:11:58,000
Okay, I'll try that.

1208
01:11:59,125 --> 01:12:01,416
But I promise,
we're on the same page together.

1209
01:12:01,500 --> 01:12:03,375
-[Beca] <i>We're having a party.</i>
-What?

1210
01:12:03,458 --> 01:12:05,875
Yeah, a party.
Since my parents are still away.

1211
01:12:05,958 --> 01:12:10,083
Not everyone has an apartment that you
can throw a party in. I really like it.

1212
01:12:10,166 --> 01:12:12,875
DAY 12

1213
01:12:12,958 --> 01:12:15,541
You know that I love parties, right?
I just love them.

1214
01:12:15,625 --> 01:12:18,333
No one's gonna throw a bucket
of pig's blood all over you.

1215
01:12:18,416 --> 01:12:20,166
You never know what can happen.

1216
01:12:20,250 --> 01:12:22,541
And even if they do, it'll get on me.

1217
01:12:22,625 --> 01:12:25,166
Because I'm going
to be glued to you all night.

1218
01:12:25,666 --> 01:12:28,750
-Beca] Awwww!
-[Melissa] Aww, that is so cute!

1219
01:12:28,833 --> 01:12:30,458
-[cell phone rings]
-[Beca] Hold this.

1220
01:12:30,541 --> 01:12:33,083
What can I do to help, guys?
I'll be the hype man.

1221
01:12:33,166 --> 01:12:36,375
Hey, wait. Guys, be quiet.
It's my mom. Hold on. Hold on, guys!

1222
01:12:36,458 --> 01:12:37,500
Hey, ma.

1223
01:12:37,583 --> 01:12:41,708
[Sandra] <i>Oh, honey, just look</i>
<i>at this horrible view that I'm stuck with.</i>

1224
01:12:41,791 --> 01:12:44,166
Look at this boring view, Caio.

1225
01:12:44,250 --> 01:12:46,041
I'm at a restaurant just off…

1226
01:12:46,541 --> 01:12:49,250
-Are you at the house, Caio?
-[Caio] <i>Yeah.</i>

1227
01:12:49,333 --> 01:12:50,875
I came to get some clean underwear.

1228
01:12:50,958 --> 01:12:54,291
[Sandra] <i>Clean underwear? No, Caio,</i>
<i>I packed you a pair for every day.</i>

1229
01:12:54,375 --> 01:12:58,875
-Caio, is someone over there?
-[Caio] <i>No, there's nobody here.</i>

1230
01:12:58,958 --> 01:13:01,541
Yeah, I just came over here.

1231
01:13:01,625 --> 01:13:03,416
[whimsical music playing]

1232
01:13:03,500 --> 01:13:06,166
It's all good. I just came over
to get some underwear.

1233
01:13:06,250 --> 01:13:07,708
<i>I'm going back to Rita's now.</i>

1234
01:13:07,791 --> 01:13:11,416
Oh, well, all right. Fine. I'll just
try calling later. Love you. Ciao.

1235
01:13:14,083 --> 01:13:15,666
[music stops]

1236
01:13:19,875 --> 01:13:21,291
Oh, God!

1237
01:13:21,375 --> 01:13:22,666
Don't say anything.

1238
01:13:22,750 --> 01:13:24,250
Mm. Say what?

1239
01:13:24,333 --> 01:13:26,750
You were gonna say I look good.
There's no need.

1240
01:13:28,916 --> 01:13:30,416
All right, mother, go ahead.

1241
01:13:30,500 --> 01:13:31,958
Aww!

1242
01:13:32,041 --> 01:13:34,166
You look so cute.

1243
01:13:34,250 --> 01:13:35,916
Oh, you're so handsome.

1244
01:13:37,625 --> 01:13:39,625
And he'll think the same thing, too.

1245
01:13:42,583 --> 01:13:44,375
I'm your mother give me some credit.

1246
01:13:45,041 --> 01:13:46,958
You think I don't notice these things?

1247
01:13:47,041 --> 01:13:48,666
[chuckles] Mom.

1248
01:13:48,750 --> 01:13:51,666
Oh. You look so handsome.

1249
01:13:51,750 --> 01:13:52,916
[Felipe] Mmm.

1250
01:13:53,625 --> 01:13:57,375
-["Carnaval" by Marina Sena playing]
-[people cheering]

1251
01:13:57,458 --> 01:14:00,041
[lyrics in Portuguese]

1252
01:14:13,666 --> 01:14:14,750
Hey.

1253
01:14:16,541 --> 01:14:17,958
It looks good, doesn't it?

1254
01:14:18,041 --> 01:14:19,750
Yeah, it all looks great!

1255
01:14:20,708 --> 01:14:22,625
-You look really good.
-[Caio] Thanks.

1256
01:14:22,708 --> 01:14:25,166
This wouldn't have happened
if it wasn't for you.

1257
01:14:28,916 --> 01:14:31,750
["K.O." by Pabllo Vittar playing]

1258
01:14:35,208 --> 01:14:38,125
-Come dance with me.
-Give me a minute, you want a drink?

1259
01:14:38,208 --> 01:14:40,625
-Can you get me another?
-Yeah, you bet.

1260
01:14:40,708 --> 01:14:42,875
[lyrics in Portuguese]

1261
01:14:46,541 --> 01:14:47,541
Hey, what's up?

1262
01:14:47,625 --> 01:14:49,833
-Oh, you know.
-Check out how many people showed.

1263
01:14:49,916 --> 01:14:51,458
People in this town are bored.

1264
01:14:52,708 --> 01:14:55,666
-This is a good song. You coming?
-In a little while.

1265
01:15:06,750 --> 01:15:09,833
[groans] I can't believe
Caio invited that guy.

1266
01:15:11,666 --> 01:15:12,625
Hello!

1267
01:15:12,708 --> 01:15:15,583
Caio has terrible taste
in friends, apart from us.

1268
01:15:15,666 --> 01:15:18,708
And you too, of course.
Obviously, you seem great.

1269
01:15:22,208 --> 01:15:24,833
-Let's go dance.
-[Melissa] Come with us.

1270
01:15:41,041 --> 01:15:43,625
[moody ethereal music playing]

1271
01:15:56,625 --> 01:15:59,000
Felipe! Felipe!

1272
01:15:59,083 --> 01:16:00,291
-What's wrong?
-Let go.

1273
01:16:03,166 --> 01:16:04,583
Where's Felipe?

1274
01:16:12,791 --> 01:16:14,875
[alarm blares]

1275
01:16:19,041 --> 01:16:21,041
[sirens blare]

1276
01:16:22,625 --> 01:16:25,333
-[Beca] I don't understand.
-How did the alarm go off?

1277
01:16:25,416 --> 01:16:27,000
Caio kissed another boy.

1278
01:16:27,083 --> 01:16:28,416
And Felipe saw.

1279
01:16:28,916 --> 01:16:31,416
What? Oh, no.

1280
01:16:37,416 --> 01:16:38,916
Felipe, what happened?

1281
01:16:39,000 --> 01:16:42,583
I don't want to talk to you, Caio.
Go back to that friend of yours.

1282
01:16:42,666 --> 01:16:45,291
Are you talking about Denis?
I didn't wanna kiss him.

1283
01:16:45,375 --> 01:16:48,750
Sure, of course you didn't.
It was obvious that you didn't want to.

1284
01:16:48,833 --> 01:16:50,250
I thought it was you, okay?

1285
01:16:51,083 --> 01:16:52,625
Because we look so similar?

1286
01:16:53,708 --> 01:16:55,791
Caio, I'm not an idiot, you know?

1287
01:16:56,291 --> 01:16:58,791
When I saw you at the party
you kissed me on the cheek.

1288
01:16:59,416 --> 01:17:02,958
I know why it's so hard for me
to come out. Everyone already knows.

1289
01:17:03,041 --> 01:17:04,791
They can see it from a mile away.

1290
01:17:04,875 --> 01:17:07,333
[Caio] You're the one
who broke up the party.

1291
01:17:07,416 --> 01:17:09,958
Think it's easy for me
to kiss another guy in front of everyone?

1292
01:17:10,041 --> 01:17:11,375
Then Denis is the lucky one.

1293
01:17:12,250 --> 01:17:14,041
Would you just listen for a second?

1294
01:17:14,125 --> 01:17:15,791
[car engine starts]

1295
01:17:15,875 --> 01:17:18,625
[moody dramatic music playing]

1296
01:17:18,708 --> 01:17:20,708
-[police siren blaring]
-No, I won't.

1297
01:17:25,333 --> 01:17:26,583
[Rita] Felipe.

1298
01:17:34,250 --> 01:17:36,041
[Felipe sobs]

1299
01:18:02,000 --> 01:18:04,250
[music becomes quiet]

1300
01:18:10,458 --> 01:18:12,500
[music becomes mysterious]

1301
01:18:16,375 --> 01:18:17,958
[music fades]

1302
01:18:18,916 --> 01:18:19,958
Sweetie?

1303
01:18:22,791 --> 01:18:27,333
DAY 13

1304
01:18:27,416 --> 01:18:31,125
[distant people chatter and shout]

1305
01:18:32,666 --> 01:18:36,375
Caio's parents came back early
because of this whole mess.

1306
01:18:37,416 --> 01:18:40,625
He said he was the one
who pulled the fire alarm, did you know?

1307
01:18:45,458 --> 01:18:47,041
Caio left already.

1308
01:18:48,958 --> 01:18:50,416
Well, it's a shame.

1309
01:18:50,500 --> 01:18:53,166
Because he'll miss Musical Wednesday now.

1310
01:18:56,833 --> 01:18:59,375
Felipe, Beca already told me
what happened.

1311
01:18:59,916 --> 01:19:02,291
-[Felipe shudders]
-I know how you must feel.

1312
01:19:02,375 --> 01:19:03,750
No, you don't know!

1313
01:19:03,833 --> 01:19:05,833
You have no idea
what I'm feeling right now.

1314
01:19:05,916 --> 01:19:09,500
Come on. Everybody gets their heart
broken when they're a teenager.

1315
01:19:09,583 --> 01:19:13,250
And you are beautiful,
and incredible, and intelligent,

1316
01:19:13,333 --> 01:19:16,041
-and you have to know that--
-Stop, Mom! Stop lying!

1317
01:19:16,125 --> 01:19:18,375
-What?
-You don't think I'm beautiful, Mom.

1318
01:19:18,458 --> 01:19:21,458
I do. I think you're the most
beautiful thing in the world.

1319
01:19:21,541 --> 01:19:23,041
What are you talking about?

1320
01:19:23,583 --> 01:19:26,916
Please Mom, just stop.
You don't think I'm beautiful.

1321
01:19:28,000 --> 01:19:31,041
If you did, you wouldn't
ever stop me from eating junk.

1322
01:19:31,666 --> 01:19:34,583
-You wouldn't worry about my health.
-What are you talking about?

1323
01:19:34,666 --> 01:19:38,083
And what do you know about love, Mom?
Even Dad didn't want you.

1324
01:19:38,166 --> 01:19:40,500
[moody music playing]

1325
01:19:53,125 --> 01:19:54,291
[sniffles]

1326
01:19:55,500 --> 01:19:57,458
[Felipe sobs]

1327
01:20:10,791 --> 01:20:13,583
[moody music becomes spirited]

1328
01:20:34,833 --> 01:20:37,208
[music fades]

1329
01:21:02,875 --> 01:21:04,958
[heartfelt music playing]

1330
01:21:17,416 --> 01:21:23,583
DAY 14

1331
01:21:23,666 --> 01:21:25,375
[music fades]

1332
01:21:25,458 --> 01:21:26,791
[door creaks]

1333
01:21:27,875 --> 01:21:29,083
[knocking]

1334
01:21:29,166 --> 01:21:30,416
[door opens]

1335
01:21:31,291 --> 01:21:32,833
[Felipe] Can I come in, Mom?

1336
01:21:35,333 --> 01:21:36,833
Of course, sweetheart.

1337
01:21:48,541 --> 01:21:50,041
I'm such an idiot.

1338
01:21:52,166 --> 01:21:54,875
I'm sorry, I never meant
to say that to you, okay?

1339
01:21:55,708 --> 01:21:57,041
I'm really sorry.

1340
01:21:59,166 --> 01:22:02,500
Sweetheart, we say the worst things
when we're angry.

1341
01:22:03,583 --> 01:22:05,666
Yeah, but that's no excuse, Mom.

1342
01:22:05,750 --> 01:22:08,625
[contemplative music playing]

1343
01:22:11,166 --> 01:22:12,708
You really like this guy.

1344
01:22:15,458 --> 01:22:18,500
Yeah, well, relationships are complicated.

1345
01:22:19,708 --> 01:22:21,375
I've been through a lot.

1346
01:22:25,833 --> 01:22:29,708
But I really feel like now,
my morale is up.

1347
01:22:29,791 --> 01:22:31,250
I'm doing much better.

1348
01:22:32,166 --> 01:22:36,791
And even so, I still get upset
when things don't work out.

1349
01:22:37,291 --> 01:22:39,458
Well, then that's their loss though.

1350
01:22:42,000 --> 01:22:43,375
It sure is.

1351
01:22:47,333 --> 01:22:49,625
And I am never going to let…

1352
01:22:51,000 --> 01:22:54,833
just a few bad apples
ever make me give up on love anymore.

1353
01:22:55,583 --> 01:22:57,791
You sound like one of your K-dramas.

1354
01:22:58,291 --> 01:22:59,916
You know what I meant.

1355
01:23:03,083 --> 01:23:04,958
I guess what I'm saying…

1356
01:23:06,750 --> 01:23:08,666
is never give up on yourself.

1357
01:23:09,583 --> 01:23:13,250
You can't throw in the towel
already just because of this heartbreak.

1358
01:23:15,000 --> 01:23:17,583
But let me give you
one piece of advice, son…

1359
01:23:20,875 --> 01:23:24,416
Never let yourself fall in love
with someone who…

1360
01:23:25,958 --> 01:23:28,458
who doesn't make you feel
like you're beautiful.

1361
01:23:31,083 --> 01:23:32,250
You too, promise?

1362
01:23:35,166 --> 01:23:36,250
Mom,

1363
01:23:37,083 --> 01:23:38,333
-I love you.
-I love you.

1364
01:23:38,416 --> 01:23:39,416
I do.

1365
01:23:43,708 --> 01:23:45,000
Come on, let's see.

1366
01:23:51,666 --> 01:23:53,541
"Revenge won't make you feel whole."

1367
01:23:53,625 --> 01:23:55,875
"It poisons and kills the soul. "

1368
01:23:55,958 --> 01:23:58,666
Wow, your grandma's doing
Chaves impressions now.

1369
01:23:58,750 --> 01:24:01,625
-Chaves? Who's Chaves?
-Chaves, from the TV show. Chaves.

1370
01:24:01,708 --> 01:24:04,458
-You really haven't heard of him?
-I still don't know.

1371
01:24:09,500 --> 01:24:11,708
-What's up?
-Don't look. No, Don't look.

1372
01:24:13,000 --> 01:24:15,750
The architect, slash, writer,
slash, pilot is over there.

1373
01:24:15,833 --> 01:24:18,125
-He's here?
-Yeah, don't look though, all right?

1374
01:24:18,208 --> 01:24:21,291
[intriguing music]

1375
01:24:24,458 --> 01:24:26,791
-Sneakers, sports jersey? You kidding me?
-Shh!

1376
01:24:26,875 --> 01:24:29,500
I can't believe you actually
cried over a man like that.

1377
01:24:29,583 --> 01:24:31,041
[Rita] What are you doing?

1378
01:24:31,125 --> 01:24:34,041
Just so you know, you missed out
on an amazing woman, know that?

1379
01:24:34,125 --> 01:24:37,125
-Uh, I'm sorry, do I know you?
-How can you treat people like?

1380
01:24:37,208 --> 01:24:40,041
-[man] Uh… Listen, I…
-No, no, you have nothing to say! Shh!

1381
01:24:40,625 --> 01:24:43,666
Ah, right. Look, it's nothing personal.
I just sort of had a--

1382
01:24:43,750 --> 01:24:47,000
Didn't you hear my son?
I have nothing to say to you.

1383
01:24:53,833 --> 01:24:56,541
[gentle whimsical music playing]

1384
01:25:01,958 --> 01:25:03,958
[both chuckling]

1385
01:25:09,875 --> 01:25:11,833
-[Felipe] Ah.
-Thanks.

1386
01:25:11,916 --> 01:25:14,833
I don't wanna see you get upset
over someone like that.

1387
01:25:15,458 --> 01:25:18,666
You're way too beautiful.
Those bangs are iconic.

1388
01:25:18,750 --> 01:25:21,125
[Rita chuckles]

1389
01:25:21,208 --> 01:25:22,375
You know what I want?

1390
01:25:22,458 --> 01:25:24,250
For me to go and assault the guy?

1391
01:25:24,333 --> 01:25:25,666
No!

1392
01:25:25,750 --> 01:25:28,875
For you to be exactly who you are,
but kind to yourself.

1393
01:25:31,291 --> 01:25:34,333
[gentle upbeat music playing]

1394
01:25:49,208 --> 01:25:55,500
I LOVE HAVING FRIENDS

1395
01:25:59,500 --> 01:26:02,916
[Sandra] He's not replying to messages,
so he might not have his phone.

1396
01:26:03,000 --> 01:26:06,375
-Thank you. What was his friend's name?
-I tried tracking his phone.

1397
01:26:06,458 --> 01:26:07,458
Uh, Lígia.

1398
01:26:07,958 --> 01:26:09,625
Uh, no, um, I forgot the phone--

1399
01:26:09,708 --> 01:26:12,750
-Beca. What about Beca?
-[Sandra] I don't like Beca.

1400
01:26:12,833 --> 01:26:14,875
-Sandra, listen--
-God, we had a fight!

1401
01:26:16,000 --> 01:26:18,708
We had a fight yesterday,
and when I woke up…

1402
01:26:19,833 --> 01:26:22,666
-He had disappeared. He took a whole bag.
-I know.

1403
01:26:22,750 --> 01:26:26,125
[Mauro] You have a fight that's one thing,
him disappearing is another.

1404
01:26:26,208 --> 01:26:29,458
[Sandra] I don't know. I already…
I… I already tried calling that…

1405
01:26:29,541 --> 01:26:30,583
What's going on?

1406
01:26:30,666 --> 01:26:33,000
Have you spoken to my son?
Has he called you?

1407
01:26:33,083 --> 01:26:35,375
No. No, I haven't talked to him. Why?

1408
01:26:35,458 --> 01:26:37,916
Roberto has a friend
at the police department, I'll call.

1409
01:26:38,000 --> 01:26:41,541
-Are you sure you haven't heard from him?
-No. No, I haven't.

1410
01:26:41,625 --> 01:26:44,208
[Mauro] If there's been an accident,
police can help.

1411
01:26:44,291 --> 01:26:46,583
-[Rita] Maybe he's with friends.
-[Mauro] Just protocol.

1412
01:26:46,666 --> 01:26:49,625
[Sandra] He doesn't have any.
-[Rita] Where does he go when he's upset?

1413
01:26:49,708 --> 01:26:51,875
[dramatic music playing]

1414
01:26:56,250 --> 01:26:59,208
[music swelling]

1415
01:27:07,250 --> 01:27:09,416
-[music becomes mysterious]
-[panting]

1416
01:27:15,375 --> 01:27:18,041
[Caio] <i>I just wish I had the courage</i>
<i>to leave the Shire.</i>

1417
01:27:18,125 --> 01:27:19,291
Leave the Shire…

1418
01:27:19,375 --> 01:27:22,583
[Caio] <i>Go on adventures.</i>
<i>And do all the things I didn't do…</i>

1419
01:27:22,666 --> 01:27:24,083
[ringing]

1420
01:27:24,666 --> 01:27:26,416
Hey, I need you over here!

1421
01:27:26,500 --> 01:27:28,041
Right Now. Hurry!

1422
01:27:29,833 --> 01:27:32,166
DAY 15

1423
01:27:32,250 --> 01:27:34,791
[spirited upbeat music playing]

1424
01:27:37,625 --> 01:27:39,583
[Beca] This town never has traffic.

1425
01:27:39,666 --> 01:27:40,583
[tires screech]

1426
01:27:40,666 --> 01:27:42,541
-Beca!
-Shit, I'm sorry.

1427
01:27:42,625 --> 01:27:44,041
[car horns honk]

1428
01:27:44,125 --> 01:27:45,666
What's going on?

1429
01:27:47,083 --> 01:27:48,625
[people shouting]

1430
01:27:49,250 --> 01:27:50,791
-Wait, Felipe! Felipe!
-Felipe!

1431
01:27:51,333 --> 01:27:53,083
Watch out for cars, Felipe!

1432
01:27:57,791 --> 01:28:00,791
[Felipe] <i>Here I am, in a romantic comedy.</i>

1433
01:28:00,875 --> 01:28:02,000
<i>Again.</i>

1434
01:28:03,250 --> 01:28:06,750
<i>Only this time,</i>
<i>the protagonist in the story is me.</i>

1435
01:28:06,833 --> 01:28:09,291
Caio! Caio! Don't get on that bus!

1436
01:28:09,375 --> 01:28:11,166
[music fades]

1437
01:28:12,750 --> 01:28:14,375
What the hell are you doing?

1438
01:28:15,541 --> 01:28:18,458
I can't stay in that house anymore.
I've got an Aunt in Sao Paolo.

1439
01:28:18,541 --> 01:28:20,208
I don't know, I'll figure it out.

1440
01:28:20,291 --> 01:28:23,375
Someone once told me that running
from problems doesn't solve anything.

1441
01:28:23,458 --> 01:28:24,791
Well, this is different.

1442
01:28:24,875 --> 01:28:27,958
Caio, I saw your mom.
She's really worried.

1443
01:28:28,458 --> 01:28:30,291
Good. That was the plan.

1444
01:28:31,458 --> 01:28:32,583
[horn honks]

1445
01:28:32,666 --> 01:28:35,750
-I'm sorry, I gotta go.
-Caio, you can't go, all right?

1446
01:28:37,291 --> 01:28:38,833
People are staring, Felipe.

1447
01:28:38,916 --> 01:28:41,125
So what? I don't care. I don't care!

1448
01:28:41,208 --> 01:28:43,291
I don't give a shit if people are staring!

1449
01:28:43,375 --> 01:28:45,791
[contemplative music playing]

1450
01:28:45,875 --> 01:28:49,250
I've spent my whole life
worrying about what others would say.

1451
01:28:51,208 --> 01:28:54,333
I thought that staying hidden in my room
would solve it all somehow.

1452
01:28:54,416 --> 01:28:56,666
But you changed that, too, Caio.

1453
01:28:57,166 --> 01:28:59,833
Because of you,
I'm not afraid. So thank you.

1454
01:29:00,708 --> 01:29:03,416
It's okay if you wanna be
with other guys. I don't care--

1455
01:29:03,500 --> 01:29:05,625
-I don't care about other guys.
-[horn honks]

1456
01:29:05,708 --> 01:29:06,916
[bus engine revs]

1457
01:29:07,000 --> 01:29:09,125
I just… I want you to stay.

1458
01:29:09,208 --> 01:29:11,958
I don't care if you're my boyfriend,
I just wanna be with you.

1459
01:29:13,166 --> 01:29:14,916
[honks horn]

1460
01:29:15,000 --> 01:29:17,041
Look, I've embarrassed myself enough

1461
01:29:17,125 --> 01:29:19,208
and don't know what to say, so--

1462
01:29:19,291 --> 01:29:21,958
[music becomes uplifting]

1463
01:29:24,750 --> 01:29:27,875
-[Beca gasps]
-[Melissa] Ahh!

1464
01:29:27,958 --> 01:29:29,583
[bus hisses]

1465
01:29:34,208 --> 01:29:36,083
-Maybe you saw a suitcase…
-I don't think so.

1466
01:29:36,166 --> 01:29:38,750
A backpack. It was a backpack…

1467
01:29:38,833 --> 01:29:42,500
We've established that there was a bag.
The question is where is he going.

1468
01:29:42,583 --> 01:29:44,416
-He didn't take a lot--
-There you are!

1469
01:29:44,500 --> 01:29:48,000
Caio! Where did you run off to, Caio?
Where in the hell did you go?

1470
01:29:48,083 --> 01:29:50,666
How could you do something like that?
Look at your mother!

1471
01:29:50,750 --> 01:29:54,166
-She's distraught. How could you run away?
-You weren't at the house!

1472
01:29:54,250 --> 01:29:55,458
I'm done running.

1473
01:29:56,625 --> 01:29:58,208
I won't run away again.

1474
01:30:02,166 --> 01:30:05,333
[contemplative music playing]

1475
01:30:05,416 --> 01:30:06,625
What are you…?

1476
01:30:07,625 --> 01:30:09,625
You're trying to piss me off, Caio?

1477
01:30:10,125 --> 01:30:12,083
Did you know about this, Rita?

1478
01:30:13,000 --> 01:30:14,708
That they like each other?

1479
01:30:15,958 --> 01:30:18,250
-Yeah, of course.
Of course.

1480
01:30:19,625 --> 01:30:22,916
Of course you knew,
and you encouraged it too, didn't you?

1481
01:30:23,000 --> 01:30:25,791
-Not at all. We can talk about it.
-I don't wanna talk about it!

1482
01:30:25,875 --> 01:30:28,041
-I don't want to talk to anyone at all.
-Okay.

1483
01:30:28,125 --> 01:30:29,500
I'm the stupid one.

1484
01:30:29,583 --> 01:30:30,666
Mom.

1485
01:30:32,208 --> 01:30:33,500
We're dating.

1486
01:30:34,083 --> 01:30:35,125
We are?

1487
01:30:35,625 --> 01:30:36,916
We are.

1488
01:30:39,541 --> 01:30:42,666
I won't run away again,
but only if you can accept me.

1489
01:30:42,750 --> 01:30:43,958
I need you to.

1490
01:30:46,166 --> 01:30:47,791
We don't recognize you.

1491
01:30:47,875 --> 01:30:50,500
-It's like we don't even know you!
-I haven't changed.

1492
01:30:52,958 --> 01:30:54,583
I'm just tired of hiding.

1493
01:30:56,833 --> 01:30:59,041
This is who I've always been.

1494
01:30:59,750 --> 01:31:02,291
All right, look, why don't you… Mauro!

1495
01:31:02,375 --> 01:31:04,958
Say something to your son. Tell him. Now!

1496
01:31:06,333 --> 01:31:09,625
You aren't gonna say anything?
You have to say something, God!

1497
01:31:12,291 --> 01:31:13,791
Are you happy, son?

1498
01:31:20,166 --> 01:31:21,583
Well, then it's fine.

1499
01:31:22,208 --> 01:31:25,333
No, it's not fine,
it's not fine. No, it's not fine.

1500
01:31:25,416 --> 01:31:27,750
No, it's not fine, Mauro.

1501
01:31:28,250 --> 01:31:31,375
Mauro, for God's sake, look at me.
You have to talk to your son,

1502
01:31:31,458 --> 01:31:33,250
You… He's… He's gonna suffer!

1503
01:31:33,333 --> 01:31:34,833
-He's gonna suffer.
-Sandra.

1504
01:31:35,958 --> 01:31:37,000
Sandra.

1505
01:31:37,875 --> 01:31:40,500
What if…?

1506
01:31:40,583 --> 01:31:42,375
[whispering] No, no. No, no.

1507
01:31:51,291 --> 01:31:53,208
Just promise me one thing.

1508
01:31:55,125 --> 01:31:57,500
Don't ever run away from us again, okay?

1509
01:32:04,500 --> 01:32:07,250
[upbeat music playing]

1510
01:32:17,166 --> 01:32:18,375
[Felipe chuckles]

1511
01:32:19,041 --> 01:32:20,708
What does your grandma say today?

1512
01:32:31,833 --> 01:32:33,583
"The whole world is yours."

1513
01:32:35,041 --> 01:32:36,083
It's ours.

1514
01:32:41,250 --> 01:32:44,416
My therapist gave me
the most boring assignment ever.

1515
01:32:45,500 --> 01:32:48,291
Here are 15 things I learned
in the last 15 days.

1516
01:32:48,375 --> 01:32:49,875
Oh, this could be a while.

1517
01:32:49,958 --> 01:32:51,791
Oh? May I?

1518
01:32:51,875 --> 01:32:53,000
Go ahead.

1519
01:32:54,458 --> 01:32:58,333
"I really like when we talk.
And I like watching TV with you."

1520
01:32:58,416 --> 01:33:01,583
<i>"I like going out on errands</i>
<i>and dancing."</i>

1521
01:33:03,000 --> 01:33:04,541
<i>"I even like playing dodgeball."</i>

1522
01:33:04,625 --> 01:33:06,333
-[chuckles]
-[kids cheer]

1523
01:33:06,416 --> 01:33:09,083
<i>"Turns out I really,</i>
<i>really like having friends."</i>

1524
01:33:09,666 --> 01:33:12,375
<i>"I like spending the whole day</i>
<i>with them, Doing nothing."</i>

1525
01:33:13,166 --> 01:33:16,458
<i>"I learned that I don't look bad</i>
<i>in plaid or red."</i>

1526
01:33:16,541 --> 01:33:20,208
"And getting drunk on persimmon
liqueur is possible."

1527
01:33:20,291 --> 01:33:21,250
[chuckles]

1528
01:33:21,916 --> 01:33:24,541
<i>"I learned that I can be strong</i>
<i>when I need to be."</i>

1529
01:33:25,375 --> 01:33:28,500
<i>"But it's okay to ask for a hug</i>
<i>when things are tough."</i>

1530
01:33:31,583 --> 01:33:32,625
That's all?

1531
01:33:35,583 --> 01:33:37,875
I love those sailor pajamas
with the little shorts.

1532
01:33:37,958 --> 01:33:40,166
[both chuckle]

1533
01:33:42,958 --> 01:33:46,166
I also like hearing you talk
about the things that you like.

1534
01:33:49,666 --> 01:33:51,250
<i>I like kissing you</i>

1535
01:33:52,083 --> 01:33:53,500
<i>and touching you.</i>

1536
01:33:58,583 --> 01:34:01,291
And you, you are

1537
01:34:02,541 --> 01:34:04,500
everything I want and more.

1538
01:34:06,291 --> 01:34:07,500
[sniffles]

1539
01:34:08,375 --> 01:34:09,500
Thank you.

1540
01:34:10,166 --> 01:34:12,208
[Felipe sniffles]

1541
01:34:12,291 --> 01:34:14,708
By my count,
there's still one thing missing.

1542
01:34:17,708 --> 01:34:19,083
Do you trust me?

1543
01:34:20,625 --> 01:34:22,791
[upbeat music continues]

1544
01:34:24,791 --> 01:34:26,125
[both chuckle]

1545
01:34:29,333 --> 01:34:30,500
[exhales deeply]

1546
01:34:42,250 --> 01:34:43,666
[both scream]

1547
01:34:43,750 --> 01:34:46,625
["Flutua" by Johnny Hooker playing]

1548
01:34:54,041 --> 01:34:56,708
[lyrics in Portuguese]

1549
01:35:12,791 --> 01:35:15,333
[Beca and Melissa squeal]

1550
01:35:17,083 --> 01:35:19,041
[Beca and Melissa laugh]

1551
01:35:37,041 --> 01:35:39,041
["Flutua" continues]

1552
01:40:04,541 --> 01:40:06,708
["Flutua" fades]